 * - At most `concurrency` tasks run simultaneously.
 * - At most `capacity` tasks are pending (waiting to run). If capacity is reached, enqueue waits until a slot frees.
 * - Cancellation distinguishes between pending (not yet started) and running (already started) tasks.
 * - AbortSignal is passed to each task's execution context.
 * - Close is idempotent; repeated close calls resolve immediately.
 * - Loader/task failures are captured and returned as rejected promises.
